@startuml
' PlugIt Architecture Overview
skinparam componentStyle rectangle
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam wrapWidth 220
skinparam maxMessageSize 200

' Network boundary to reflect PI_ALLOWED_NETWORKS
frame "Network Boundary (controlled by PI_ALLOWED_NETWORKS)" as NET {
  actor "External User /\nSystem" as External
  component "PlugIt API Client\n(init with API_URL)" as APIClient

  node "PlugIt Proxy" as Proxy {
    component "Proxy Core" as ProxyCore
    database "Proxy Data Store" as ProxyDB

    package "Mail Intake <<example/standalone>>" as MailIntake {
      component "Auto-response\nFilter" as AutoFilter
      component "Routing Token\nValidator\n(SHA-512 slice [30:42])" as TokenValidator
      component "Text Payload\nExtractor" as TextExtractor
      component "Mail Handler" as MailHandler
    }
  }
}

' Example mail processing flow (structural dataflow, not a sequence diagram)
cloud "Inbound Email" as InboundMail
InboundMail --> AutoFilter : message
AutoFilter --> TokenValidator : if not auto-response
TokenValidator --> TextExtractor : if hash valid
TextExtractor --> MailHandler : payload + routing data
MailHandler --> InboundMail : ack & delete on success

External --> ProxyCore : UI/API access via Proxy
APIClient --> ProxyCore : HTTP(S) requests\nProxy API endpoint
ProxyCore --> ProxyDB : read/write

' Services side
frame "PlugIt Services (N)" as Services {
  package "Service A" as SA {
    component "PlugIt Service A" as ServiceA
    database "Service A DB" as DBA
  }
  package "Service B" as SB {
    component "PlugIt Service B" as ServiceB
    database "Service B DB" as DBB
  }
}

' Proxy-to-service communication through the PlugIt protocol
ProxyCore --> ServiceA : PlugIt protocol
ProxyCore --> ServiceB : PlugIt protocol

' Each service uses its own configured database connection
ServiceA --> DBA : SQLALCHEMY_URL
ServiceB --> DBB : SQLALCHEMY_URL

' Migration tooling and upgrade files for schema evolution
artifact "Upgrade Files\n(migrations)" as UpgradeFiles
component "Alembic Migration\nTool" as Alembic
UpgradeFiles -down- Alembic
Alembic -down-> DBA : apply upgrades
Alembic -down-> DBB : apply upgrades

' Configuration sources
folder "Project Config\n(API_URL, SQLALCHEMY_URL,\nDEBUG, PI_BASE_URL,\nPI_ALLOWED_NETWORKS)" as CfgProject
folder "Local/Private Config\n(excluded from VCS)" as CfgLocal

CfgProject --> ServiceA : service settings
CfgProject --> ServiceB : service settings
CfgLocal --> ServiceA : private overrides
CfgLocal --> ServiceB : private overrides
CfgProject --> ProxyCore : network & proxy settings

note right of ProxyCore
- Exposes Proxy API endpoint
- Enforces PI_ALLOWED_NETWORKS
- Communicates with services via PlugIt protocol
end note

note bottom of Services
Each PlugIt Service is isolated and maintains its
own datastore and migrations.
end note

@enduml
